comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T21:43:04.919Z","harness:claude-code","Implemented all four. (1) docs/CONFIGURATION.md governance.start_blocker_enforcement row names update --status in_progress, claim --start, claim --next --start and start-task, and says claim --next --start skips a refused candidate; docs/COMMANDS.md documents start_refused. (2) ItemRevisionConflictRowFields is exported from the SDK root; sdk/public-surface.json records it as an additive symbol. (3) claimNextFromRecommendations (src/sdk/lifecycle/claim.ts) skips a candidate refused with start_blocked_by_open_dependency (the refusal fires inside the claim's locked mutation, so nothing is written to it), claims the next candidate, and reports skipped ids as start_refused on the available and if-available results and in details.start_refused of the exhausted refusal, whose why now distinguishes start refusals from claims by other agents. Spec: tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/start-race.spec.ts drives a real tracker where the blocker edge lands after ranking; the refused candidate's history is unchanged. (4) postCloseDependentConflict (src/sdk/lifecycle/close.ts) replaces the dependent conflict's required/nextSteps: the close is complete and must not be retried, and the only remaining step is re-reading and unblocking the dependent with pm update <dep> --status open --unset blocked_by --unset blocked_reason --expect-hash <dep>=<item_hash>. That command was verified in a sandbox (status open, blocked_by edge removed). Spec assertions in tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/item-revision.spec.ts."
  "2026-11-03T22:55:04.913Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 1, fixed: three P2s on the post-close dependent remedy. Recovery commands now carry the caller's tracker scope (--pm-path, --no-extensions) from resolvePmCommandScopeArgs; the unblock uses the configured statusRegistry.open_status instead of a hardcoded open; and the remedy covers every dependent the fan-out left blocked (details.pending_unblock, one get+update step pair per id), not only the first conflict. The conflict is enriched with changes_since before pending_unblock joins its details, so the evidence is kept."
