body: "The CodeRabbit full review of PR 1654 (10:24Z, head 9e5407474) left four Minor findings. They were deferred under the bot-loop convergence rule so the PR could merge on green CI. Each one was checked against the code.\n1. docs/CONFIGURATION.md: the governance.start_blocker_enforcement row lists only update --status in_progress and claim --start. It omits claim --next --start and start-task, which take the same admission check.\n2. sdk/public-surface.json: ItemRevisionConflictRowFields is not an exported snapshot symbol, so the snapshot cannot detect changes to the inherited conflict fields on bulk and history rows.\n3. src/sdk/lifecycle/claim.ts: in the claim --next candidate loop, any error other than already_claimed_by is rethrown. A candidate whose blocker opens between ranking and the locked start therefore ends the pass, and later healthy candidates are not attempted. The refused candidate is not written.\n4. src/sdk/lifecycle/close.ts: the post-close dependent revision conflict spreads the dependent conflict's required/nextSteps text. That text tells the caller to retry the close with --expect-hash, but the close has already committed, and a repeat close is refused as terminal without --force."
